   "properties": {},
   "widgets_values": [
    "1. For each model: upload their image (from 'Character creation', or any photo where the face is clear), give a name, and describe body and clothes (paste the Body and Clothes text from 'Character creation'). Model 1 is on the LEFT of the picture, Model 2 on the RIGHT.\n2. Describe the action and the camera angle.\n3. Optional: to copy the poses from a reference photo, right-click the green 'Action reference' group > Bypass Group Nodes (turns it on), and load the photo. Put the person on the left of the photo in Model 1's place.\n4. Queue. Two variations are saved as outputs/comfyui/scenes/<Name1>_<Name2>_00001_.png\n\nThe face swap needs a visible face: if one is turned away, try another seed or ask for it in the camera text (e.g. 'both faces visible')."
   ],
   "title": "How to use",
   "color": "#432",
   "bgcolor": "#653"
